{"type": "message", "id": "86f3972d", "parentId": "2bbb2af0", "timestamp": "2026-04-16T16:16:19.493Z", "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "thinking", "thinking": "I found some data. From the search results:\n\nFrom the SEC filing (last10k.com):\n\"Total revenues 16,934 21,454 24,318 23,329 24,927\"\n\nThis appears to be showing quarterly revenues in millions. Let me try to figure out the sequence. Looking at the data:\n- 16,934 - appears to be Q2 2022\n- 21,454 - appears to be Q3 2022\n- 24,318 - appears to be Q4 2022\n- 23,329 - appears to be Q1 2023\n- 24,927 - appears to be Q2 2023\n\nSo from Q2 2023 filing (which includes prior quarter comparisons):\n- Q1 2023 revenue: $23,329 million (or $23.33 billion)\n- Q2 2023 revenue: $24,927 million (or $24.93 billion)\n\nI already have from earlier search:\n- Q1 2023: net income $2,539 million, revenue ~$23.33 billion\n- Q2 2023: net income $2,614 million, revenue ~$24.93 billion\n- Q3 2023: net income $1,878 million\n- Q4 2023: net income $7,943 million\n\nNow I need to find Q3 and Q4 2023 revenues. Let me search for those.", "thinkingSignature": "reasoning_content"}, {"type": "text", "text": "I found Q1 and Q2 revenue data. Let me search for Q3 and Q4 2023 revenue figures."}, {"type": "toolCall", "id": "tool-139825f9255642d38a22bb827c0691f8", "name": "web_search", "arguments": {"count": 10, "query": "Tesla Q3 2023 quarterly revenue total $24.9 billion earnings September 30 SEC"}}, {"type": "toolCall", "id": "tool-ee3d3d92096a4023b3497ced8cfe1130", "name": "web_search", "arguments": {"count": 10, "query": "Tesla Q4 2023 quarterly revenue total December 31 earnings $25.1 billion"}}], "api": "openai-completions", "provider": "qwen", "model": "glm-5", "usage": {"input": 72454, "output": 734, "cacheRead": 14271, "cacheWrite": 0, "totalTokens": 87459, "cost": {"input": 0, "output": 0, "cacheRead": 0, "cacheWrite": 0, "total": 0}}, "stopReason": "toolUse", "timestamp": 1776356160397, "responseId": "chatcmpl